Trace: _initiateWithdraw first requires PT.isExpired(), then redeems exactly ptAmount of that account's PT via
  PendlePTLib.redeemExpiredPT (post-expiry PT→SY is the fixed 1:1 accrued redemption, then SY→TOKEN_OUT_SY at the
  issuer's own redeem rate — the conversion the claim says is missing is performed inside the SY redeem, not skipped).
  The resulting tokenOutSy is the real, realized token balance now held by the vault, approved to and pulled by
  withdrawRequestManager.initiateWithdraw together with account and sharesAmount: sharesHeld. That call creates a
  per-account withdraw request keyed to that account's own shares: those shares are thereafter valued from the request's
  escrowed yieldTokenAmount, not from the vault's PT balance, and the PT backing them has been removed from the vault
  in the same call. So the numerator (yield tokens leaving) and the denominator (shares removed from PT-denominated
  accounting) move together for the same account — there is no unchanged share supply left standing against a reduced PT
  balance, and no other depositor's claim is touched. The "sUSDe/USDe premium" is not a loss at all: yieldTokenAmount
  for the request is denominated in TOKEN_OUT_SY by construction and the manager settles that request in TOKEN_OUT_SY
  terms, so no cross-denomination division against PT units ever occurs. The claim also depends entirely on
  WithdrawRequestManager accounting that is not shown here; under the tie-break, unproven socialisation cannot survive.
  VERDICT|REFUTED|src/staking/PendlePT.sol:_initiateWithdraw:148|class=C22|The redeemed TOKEN_OUT_SY is escrowed in a
